  "scope_id": "SL23-BOUNDED-20261025-001",
  "title": "SL(2,3) is polynomial with bounded homology; the line is not abelian-by-nilpotent",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "SL(2,3) is polynomial on closed 3-manifolds with bounded first homology: its maps are A4 maps forming affine twisted-cocycle spaces over boundedly many maps to Z3, and the lift through the centre is obstructed by a quadratic function into the bounded group H^2(M; F2), whose zeros Gauss sums count. Since SL(2,3) is not abelian-by-nilpotent while S4 and its double covers are #P-hard, the bounded-homology line separates Fitting heights 2 and 3 as far as tested.",
